Shouldn't those be called "analysts" instead of "catalysts"? :)

When forming lujvo, it is possible to extend the literal meaning of
the components, so even if "se fusra" is limited to bio-catalysts that
facilitate catabolic reactions, that doesn't mean that "selfusra"
can't have a wider application. Perhaps "zanfusra" and "malfusra" can
distinguish the ana- and cata-bolic types.

I'm not saying this is necessarily a good idea, just that one
shouldn't be too literal-minded when forming lujvo, as long as the
structure of the relationship is respected. I have used "kijyfusra"
for "rusty", BTW.

